    <p class="eyebrow mb-3">09 / Process</p>
    <h2>My AI search optimisation process</h2>

    <p>My process has five steps. Each builds on the one before.</p>

    <h3>Step 1: entity audit and optimisation</h3>

    <p>I begin by auditing your business's entity presence across the web. I examine your website, Google Business Profile, LinkedIn, Companies House, industry directories, review platforms and any other site that mentions your business. I identify inconsistencies in your business name, address, phone number and services description. I then resolve them to create a unified entity graph. This work often starts as part of a full <a href="/audit/">SEO audit</a>. The audit includes a dedicated AI search readiness component.</p>

    <h3>Step 2: structured data implementation</h3>

    <p>I implement comprehensive JSON-LD schema markup across your website, including Organization, LocalBusiness, Service, FAQPage, Article, and BreadcrumbList schemas. This gives AI platforms machine-readable information about your business that supplements the text content they extract.</p>

    <h3>Step 3: content structure for extractability</h3>

    <p>I restructure your existing content and create new content following AI-extractable patterns: direct answers in opening sentences, proper heading hierarchies, concise paragraphs, and semantic HTML. Each page is designed to be both useful for human readers and easily parseable by AI systems.</p>

    <h3>Step 4: citation building</h3>

    <p>I build citations and mentions of your business across authoritative sources that AI platforms trust. This includes industry publications, local business directories, professional associations, and relevant content platforms. Each citation reinforces your entity authority and increases the probability of AI citation.</p>

    <h3>Step 5: crawler access</h3>

    <p>I check robots.txt and any host-level bot blocking so that Googlebot, OAI-SearchBot and PerplexityBot can reach the pages you want found. I record your decision on training crawlers separately. Google-Extended controls Gemini training only; AI Overviews use Googlebot.</p>

